{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 59, :comments ["<b>This is the law of the plague</b> — תורת המצורע. תורת אשר בו. זאת ההלכה. תורת הצרעת. — five verses corresponding to the five fifths of the Torah, to teach that one who neglects them is as if he transgresses the five fifths of the Torah. Ten sections of plagues there are, among plagues of people, plagues of garments, and plagues of houses — that if they fulfill the Ten Commandments they will be saved from these ten."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "The phrase ה' חומשין (five fifths) refers to the five books of the Torah; לשה\"ר is taken as לשה\"ר = לא שומר הרמז, rendered 'one who neglects them' based on context. The four Hebrew phrases listed are the opening formulae of the successive plague-sections."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:25.124156605Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}